      "candidate_id": "C05",
      "verdict": "true_drift",
      "reason": "The example passes a non-existent `httpx.Mounts` object to `transport=`, while the documented routing API uses a mounts dictionary passed to `Client(mounts=...)`.",
      "code_citation": {
        "path": "docs/advanced/transports.md",
        "start_line": 298,
        "end_line": 299,
        "quote": "mounts = {'http://': HTTPSRedirectTransport()}\nclient = httpx.Client(mounts=mounts)"
      },
      "suggested_doc_fix": "Replace the `httpx.Mounts` example with `mounts = {'http://': HTTPSRedirect(), 'https://': httpx.HTTPTransport()}` and `client = httpx.Client(mounts=mounts)`."
    }
  ],
  "additional_findings": [
    {
      "finding_id": "AD-1",
      "drift_kind": "signature",
      "explanation": "The mounting example uses an outdated low-level `BaseTransport.handle_request(self, method, url, headers, stream, extensions)` API and tuple return, while the documented current transport API uses `handle_request(self, request)` and returns an `httpx.Response`.",
      "doc_citation": {
        "path": "docs/advanced/transports.md",
        "start_line": 285,
        "end_line": 294,
        "quote": "    def handle_request(self, method, url, headers, stream, extensions):\n        scheme, host, port, path = url\n        if port is None:\n            location = b\"https://%s%s\" % (host, path)\n        else:\n            location = b\"https://%s:%d%s\" % (host, port, path)\n        stream = httpx.ByteStream(b\"\")\n        headers = [(b\"location\", location)]\n        extensions = {}\n        return 303, headers, stream, extensions"
      },
      "code_citation": {
        "path": "docs/advanced/transports.md",
        "start_line": 174,
        "end_line": 175,
        "quote": "    def handle_request(self, request):\n        return httpx.Response(200, json={\"text\": \"Hello, world!\"})"
      },
      "proposed_fix": "Rewrite the mounting transport example to implement `handle_request(self, request)` and return an `httpx.Response`, as shown in the custom transport example."
    }
  ]
}
